{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix implemented in worktree urson-advisory-visibility (branch off origin/main).\n\nNew module src/rebar/review_bot/finding_publish.py (211 LOC) owns the publishing surface:\n- render_findings_block(findings, kind=...) — EXTRACTED from adapter._summarize's inlined blocking enumeration, so header/truncation/overflow-note wording is defined once and both branches share it. MAX_DETAIL_CHARS=240 / MAX_ITEMS=10 promoted to named constants (the exact pre-fix limits); a test pins byte-identical output for kind='blocking'.\n- parse_anchor(location) — same rule as the pre-existing authority rebar.llm.code_review.shim._parse_location, with a reconciliation test asserting the two agree across a table of inputs so they cannot drift. Not shared outright because finding_publish must stay importable without the heavy [agents] extra.\n- partition_findings / build_inline_comments — anchorable only when the parsed path is a REAL key of the revision file map AND a line number is present; inline comments carry unresolved=false so an advisory can never hold up submission.\n- post_review(...) — casts the vote with comments attached; on GerritError retries message-only with a notice naming the durable code_review artifact. A 409 (change closed) is re-raised untouched so the voter's existing skip path is unchanged, as is a failure of a POST that carried no comments.\n\nadapter.py: _translate_findings now carries 'location' through (additive key); _summarize's PASS branch emits the finding TEXT rather than a bare count, and the 'finding' branch appends advisories too.\ngerrit_client.py: new get_revision_files (get_merge_files delegates to it, so the endpoint call exists once); post_vote gained an optional comments map, included only when non-empty.\nvoter.py: the line-700 call site now goes through post_review; 791 LOC, under the 800 cap.\ndocs/adr/0009-review-bot-pipe.md section 3 amended — it documented the outbound vote shape this change extends.\n\nRED-verified: tests/unit/test_review_bot_finding_publish.py (19 tests) failed on the missing module, then the adapter assertions failed against the count-only behaviour, before going green.\n\nNote on the plan-review advisory that predicted this: updating the duck-typed post_vote test doubles was indeed needed — four fakes across tests/unit/test_review_bot.py and tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_metrics.py. That advisory was VISIBLE to me only because the review-plan CLI prints advisories to stdout; had it come through the Gerrit surface this bug is about, I would never have seen it. That is live corroboration of the operator's report.\n\nmake lint and make typecheck both pass."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786576842297146001,"uuid":"bdabb621-cca6-4c7a-a47b-e24e622190f3"}